<article class="env-lemma" id="06M1">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06M1">Lemma <span data-tag="06M1">72.16.1</span>.</a> Let $k$ be a field. Let $X$ be an algebraic space smooth over $k$. Then $X$ is a regular algebraic space. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Choose a scheme $U$ and a surjective étale morphism $U \to X$. The morphism $U \to \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(k)$ is smooth as a composition of an étale (hence smooth) morphism and a smooth morphism (see Morphisms of Spaces, Lemmas <a href="/tag/04XX" data-tag="04XX">67.39.6</a> and <a href="/tag/03ZD" data-tag="03ZD">67.37.2</a>). Hence $U$ is regular by Varieties, Lemma <a href="/tag/056S" data-tag="056S">33.25.3</a>. By Properties of Spaces, Definition <a href="/tag/03E6" data-tag="03E6">66.7.2</a> this means that $X$ is regular. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>